From 1b8fec14a7170ee1cf6b3dcf97ab38e4480d5ff8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 22:35:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][VideoPlayer] 3D: the depth of subtitles measured in
 HDR10 and HLG too

The depth of subtitles and of the interface over a 3D video was not
measured for an HDR video: its video was drawn once for both eyes under the
composited interface, where no eye of it could be copied, and the subtitles
went to the fixed depth. Since an HDR video in 3D is drawn in the view of
each eye (the pass after the interface's, CWinSystem::VideoLayerInEachEye()),
each eye can be copied there, after it is drawn and before the subtitles
drawn with it.

- CRenderManager::Render() copies the eye in the pass that drew the video,
  the interface's or the one after it (a pass with the view OFF copies
  nothing), and tells the meter whether the video is drawn in each eye's
  view (Facts::drawnInEachEye).
- CStereoDepthMeter measures such a video; one drawn once for both eyes
  under the interface (native Dolby Vision) is still not measured, and
  kodi.log says so.
- The eye copies are matched in the signal they are in: the pictures of
  known depth of the host test, drawn in PQ (their SDR white at 203 cd/m2,
  as ITU-R BT.2408 places it) and in HLG into a framebuffer of 10 bits,
  at full light and at a quarter of it, give the depths of their SDR
  copies within 0.006 % of the width in frame packing, side by side and
  top and bottom (tools/regress/kodi-host, stage stereo, hdrdepth_gl).

The help of the setting no longer says that HDR video is not measured
(English, and es_es, es_ar, es_mx).
